From bad35aef8f249a2489d1051f7ae5249b3f39a920 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Blichmann <cblichmann@google.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:25:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Use VDSO as the wrapper for KML resource

Expose direct kernel call wrappers through the vDSO on x86_64 and ARM
when CONFIG_KERNEL_MODE_LINUX is enabled:

- Populate KML dispatch pointers (kml_trampoline, sys_call_table,
  schedule_timeout_interruptible, trace_call_by_kml) in vdso_time_data
  while preserving standard vDSO timekeeping for unprivileged Ring-3 /
  USR_MODE tasks.
- Add kml_trampoline / __kml_trampoline on x86_64 to switch GSBASE and
  RSP onto the task kernel stack in Ring 0 without privilege traps.
- Export clock_gettime, gettimeofday, sched_yield, nanosleep,
  kernel_sched_timeout, trace_call_by_kml, kml_syscall, and kml_call
  under LINUX_2.6 in the vDSO.
---
